WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.651
Run over the fixture, the rule
does catch the obvious case:

2
00:00:03.651 --> 00:00:07.712
a person adding a secret to an app
that already had a certificate.

3
00:00:07.712 --> 00:00:11.263
But three filters make it
blind in the riskiest places.

4
00:00:11.263 --> 00:00:15.562
It only looks at initiators with
an at sign, so a credential added

5
00:00:15.562 --> 00:00:20.024
by an app is never seen, including
an app abusing a broad permission.

6
00:00:20.024 --> 00:00:23.273
It drops events where the
old key list was empty,

7
00:00:23.273 --> 00:00:26.187
so the very first secret
on an app vanishes.

8
00:00:26.187 --> 00:00:28.564
And it keeps only application targets,

9
00:00:28.564 --> 00:00:32.260
so a credential added to a
service principal is dropped too.
